#section(Diffusion,Diffusion)

Since v5.22, ABackup is now a freeware program. Without written authorization, any commercial usage
or selling is absolutly forbidden. You can copy and spread this program under the following conditions:

#indent(4)
1. All the files must be provided
#break
2. No file can be modified, in any way
#break
3. You can't ask for more than 5 USD for this
#indent(0)

In spite of several tests, no warranty is made that there are no errors in ABackup. YOU USE THIS PROGRAM
AT YOUR OWN RISK. In no event I shall be liable for any damage, direct or indirect, resulting of the use
of ABackup.

#section(Introduction,Introduction)
ABackup is a program which allows you to backup data from your hard disk. It can be used
on any Amiga model, providing you have Kickstart V37 or higher, and at least 1 Mb of
memory.

ABackup has all the features you might expect from such a program:

#indent(4)
#item
- Both full and selective backup and restore operations (you can select the files
by name, by date, by protection bits, but also one by one)

#item
- Backup to floppy disks, to partitions (for example a SyQuest cartrige) or to an
archive file. Optional data compression, data encryption, verification, and archive
bit setting.

#item
- Restore to any directory, with or without restoring the original directory tree,
and handling of already existing files. Optional date and empty directories restore.

#item
- Backup of non-AmigaDOS partitions (PC, Mac, UNIX, ...)

#item
- Optional report file for all operations

#item
- Full Intuition interface, AmigaGuide documentation.
#indent(0)

However, ABackup is not just one more backup program. This program also provides
unusual features, like:

#indent(4)
#item
- Support for removable disks (SyQuest, Zip, Jaz, etc...), which are handled like
floppy disks.

#item
- Transparent support of High Density floppy disks. Cyclic utilisation of several
disks drives. Supports mixing of Double Density and High Density floppy disks.
Transparent support of the "diskspare.device".

#item
- Asynchronous writes for maximal backup speed

#item
- Data compression can be performed by the "xpk.library" or an external program.
Automatic exclusion of files already compressed.

#item
- Allows full operation automatization : you can, for example, start a backup just
with a double-click over an icon.

#item
- Lots of controls, in order to avoid data loss due to handling errors.

#item
- Supports of the "MultiUserFileSystem" : access rights and owner are automatically
backed up. When restoring files to a partition which is managed by this filesystem,
theses informations will be automatically restored.

#indent(0)

