#section(Historique,Program history)
v5.00, 15-Aug-95, 107332 bytes

#indent(0)
v5.01, 30-Sep-95, 108388 bytes
#indent(4)
#item
- Catalog rebuilding was unusuable for archives on floppy disks (terminated
without creating the new catalogue)
#item
- A few errors corrected in old archive format support (one of these errors
made failed backup which where made just after).
#item
- Using several units (DF0: and DF1: for example) now works (in v5.00, ABackup
couldn't open the second unit, because it's name was overwritten)
#item
- Added the "__stackext" directive for all recursive functions, in order to
avoid crashes by lack of stack space
#item
- Added the ECSUFFIX argument, which let you specify the suffix added by the
external compression program (so you may now use LZX)
#item
- Do not change now the comment, the icon and the protection bits of archive
files, when you do a restore or a verify operation
#item
- The message suggesting to verify the backup, when a bad cylinder has been
detected, only appears now at the end of the backup
#item
- When using a custom screen, the window opened by ABackup was too large, so
the screen's menu bar disapeared at the first WindowToFront() call
#item
- No more problems when you quit the program, and visitors windows are left
on ABackup custom screen (the screen is left opened)
#item
- When you ask to rebuild the catalog, ABackup now first display the archive
selection window (as for restore or verify), and do not ask any comment for
the catalog.
#item
- The "Preferences" gadget, on the Monitor window, is wider (the german text
did not fit in)
#item
- Do not verify now the name of the SCSI driver, in the Preferences program
(this was a problem because, if the SCSI port number was not correct, the
previous driver name was taken back)

#indent(0)
v5.02, 28-Oct-95, 108180 bytes
#indent(4)
#item
- Didn't react to the "Abort" gadget while sorting directory trees (during the
loading of the files to backup)
#item
- When "No" was answered to the request asking if the current disk could be
overwritten, the first bloc of the disk was destroyed anyway
#item
- Removed two enforcer hits at program startup (occurred only when no catalog
file was installed)
#item
- Now sets the archive bit only on successfully backed up files (no more on any
selected file)
#item
- Couldn't find the on-line help with a Kickstart version lower than V40 (used
the "language" variable, which is not defined before this version)
#item
- The disk gauge now goes up to 100% in read more (restore/verify, it used to
stop at 98%, although 100% was read)
#item
- Speeded up the filename sorting function (should be about two times faster on
directories containing several hundred of files)

#indent(0)
v5.10, 23-Dec-95, 111996 bytes
#indent(4)
#item
- Enhanced MUFS support : you can't restore or verify files for which you don't
have read access
#item
- Catalog rebuilding totally rewritten. For archives created by v5.10 or higher,
the generated catalog will be good up to 64 sub-directory levels, and 256
sub-directories per level. Things will also be better (but not perfect) for
previous archive formats.
#item
- About two times faster when reading archives (restore/verify operations)
#item
- Filename sorting algoritm changed (now takes less than two seconds to sort
a 3000 files directory, instead of more than one hour)
#item
- Selected/processed/left sizes have now a decimal (i.e. 2.6 Mb instead of 2 Mb)
#item
- Input/output buffer for streamer access can be allocated in FAST memory now.
#item
- A few bugs fixed in old archive format support
#item
- Automatic splitting of large files will now be correct even if the temporary
directory is not on RAM:
#item
- Windows where too high on a Custom screen, so the screen's menu bar could
disappear in some cases.
#item
- Added missing "__stackext" directive on two recursive functions

#indent(0)
v5.11, 03-Feb-96, 112152 bytes
#indent(4)
#item
- No longer crashes when it have to switch to another disk drive to write the
archive catalog
#item
- The "Print current list" item used to send the output to the "Ram:Toto" file,
instead of the printer

#indent(0)
v5.12, 01-May-96, 112172 bytes
#indent(4)
#item
- If the last disk was not much used, the disk header was not written at the
right location (overwrited the archive catalog instead of being written on the
first cylinder)
#item
- Did not check the length of the root name before copying it in the header blocks,
so it overwritted other data area if longer than 32 characters.
#item
- The "ARC" keyword after the "SELECT" argument had to be specified in uppercase in
order to be recognized.
#item
- Display problem when restoring/verifying a partition : the displayed size of the
last cylinder was in fact the total size of the partition
#item
- When you confirm the overwritting of an existing archive file, the DELETE and WRITE
protection bits are set before opening the file
#item
- On the selection window, links are flagged by the "Link" word instead of the file
size (like "Drawer" for the directories)

#indent(0)
