#indent(0)
#section(FAQ,Frequently Asked Questions)

#indent(2)
#item
Q:I've tried to use LZX, with external compression, but it doesn't work.
All the files are "Stored", and lots of ".lzx" files are left in the
temporary directory.
#item
A:If the external compression program adds a suffix to filenames (LZX
adds ".lzx"), you must use the ECSUFFIX argument to tell ABackup which
suffix is added.

#item
Q:At the end of a backup, I had a requester "CAUTION ! Some cylinders on
the target drive were defectives !". I thought ABackup could handle this
kind of problem, so I would not have to restart the backup again.
#item
R:This kind of error is handled by ABackup, which simply marks the bad
cylinders as "unusuable", and try to write on the next cylinder. This
message is only here to suggest you to perform a verify operation, to
make sure the backup is correct (some write errors might have not been
detected).

#indent(0)
@endbase

